      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "AR from a single photo: ArUco marker board -> calibrated 3D render\n\n1. 'CV ArUco Detect Markers' finds every DICT_6X6_250 marker on the board image (failure-tolerant: none found -> count 0, empty arrays). 'CV ArUco Draw Markers' shows what was detected.\n2. 'CV ArUco Board Pose (Average)' solves each marker's pose (IPPE_SQUARE, flip ambiguity resolved per marker) and averages them into one board pose. 'CV Camera Matrix' supplies APPROXIMATE intrinsics - fx = fy = image width, principal point = image centre - good enough for a convincing composite without any calibration session (swap in 'Calibrate Camera' / 'CV Load Camera Params' for metric accuracy). marker_length = 1 makes one marker edge the scene unit.\n3. 'CV Camera Pose To 3D View' converts K + rvec/tvec into the camera dict, orbit-anchored on the board centroid (the pose origin).\n4. 'CV 3D Object Transform' parks the model: 'model_up' turns the y-up GLB onto the board normal, and ONE set of numbers comes out in both the lanes that can carry a placement - the 'object_transform' string the viewer renders with, and a 4x4 'matrix' for 'CV Transform Points 3D'. Because the string is wired in, the viewer's gizmo only PREVIEWS a drag: this node's value wins on the next run (read a dragged placement back with 'CV Parse Object Transform').\n5. 'CV Preview 3D (Calibrated Camera)' composites the milk truck onto the photo with the exact projection, and emits its silhouette MASK and object-relative depth. 'lock camera' keeps the solved view fixed while you edit.\n\nAnnotating the model this parks - callouts clicked on the mesh, and a measured length clicked on the footage - is workflow 77.\n\nFailure-tolerant end to end: a photo without markers gives found=false, a zero pose, and the bridge falls back to a frontal default view - the render still executes (truck on empty background), no control flow needed.\n\nThe 3D model must sit in ComfyUI/input/3d/MilkTruck.glb (copy it from example_inputs/, see sources.txt)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
